
This repo is a solution to unlock carrier locked Google Pixel 8a device.
The solution was inspired by two repositories: Root-My-Pixel and Root-My-Pixel-Pixel6a.

This is the only solution for Google Pixel 8a (akita, build id: CP2A.260805.005)
The phone was locked to the T-Mobile US / Sprint network ecosystem, but configured to allow specific virtual operators (MVNOs) and sub-brands via GID1 (Group Identifier 1) codes.
See the example of output below.

What it does:
1. The ./scripts/get_root.sh gets root on locked device by two stages:
 - stage 1: gets root using CVE-2026-43499 exploit (context=u:r:kernel:s0)
 - stage 2: uses KASLR (slide) method and inserts KernelSU-Next module (context=u:r:ksu:s0)
2. The ./scripts/unlock_sim.sh unlocks carrier locked device by two stages:
 - stage 1: disables oobconfig application
 - stage 2: clears modem rules


Thid party files:
./third_party/kernelsu-next/bin/ksud-pixel - extracted from assets from Root-My-Pixel apk: assets/ksud/ksud
./third_party/exploit/akita-CP2A.260805.005.so - extracted from assets from Root-My-Pixel apk: assets/exploits/akita-CP2A.260805.005.so
./third_party/exploit/exploit-helper - taken from Root-My-Pixel-Pixel6a: binaries/cve-2026-43499-root
./third_party/kernel-symbols/akita-CP2A.260805.005.ksym.tsv - extracted by repo owner from Pixel 8a kernel image
./third_party/kernelsu-next/modules/android14-6.1_kernelsu_v3.3.0.ko - taken from Root-My-Pixel-Pixel6a: ksun/android14-6.1_kernelsu_v3.3.0.ko
